ulty":3,"explanation":"The Gospel of John does not name the soldier; Longinus comes from later Christian tradition, which also linked him to the Holy Lance.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad6a-74c6-bc71-f078a968cf51","description":"Longinus","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad6a-7796-9ea8-8969b94688d9","description":"Atticus","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6a-7a1e-a1a7-8eb04c0df5a2","description":"Augustus","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6a-7a90-a44e-df27aa74ada8","description":"Tiberius","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad6a-7a5e-87e8-e26ced6d6c98","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which philosopher famously said \'Things alter for the worse spontaneously, if they be not altered for the better designedly\'?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Bacon was also an English statesman whose emphasis on observation and experiment helped shape modern scientific inquiry.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad6a-7385-840c-d94b849a1e31","description":"Francis Bacon","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad6a-73ae-b5c2-84210ba82fe8","description":"Jean-Paul Sartre","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6a-7184-9fd9-60ed71581b8c","description":"Socrates","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6a-7f53-b93b-1d2e646f275b","description":"William of Ockham","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad6a-79b5-9178-f845e504c4a7","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which of these languages would you find spoken in Angola?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Portuguese is Angola\u2019s official language, a legacy of its colonial history.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad6a-71d6-b1e6-609a7d3c0f75","description":"Portuguese","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad6a-7253-bc43-11d3a53de883","description":"Hindi","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6a-75b3-ab2a-ef8b321cba53","description":"Berber","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6a-797e-a534-530978416f57","description":"Gujarati","corr