mis?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Leto was a Titaness and the mother of the twins she had with Zeus. Their birth on Delos is a well-known episode in Greek mythology.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7ec6-95bb-5ba59cbc3ff9","description":"Leto","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-70d3-9fc4-9dd0b2ffa23c","description":"Diana","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7c6f-970c-0333892cb19e","description":"Helen","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-718c-a01b-2827fbbef805","description":"Aphrodite","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7a18-bf1c-0252cad528fb","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which Pig Latin word is used to reject or cancel a statement?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Ixnay comes from \u201cnix,\u201d an informal word meaning to reject or prohibit; Pig Latin moves the opening consonant sound to the end and adds \u201cay.\u201d","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7424-8d66-4222522eb15b","description":"Ixnay","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7dd6-b51f-aaee8a6d5090","description":"Epay","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-73bc-ad2b-9eaa73a0a334","description":"Ocklay","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7609-b0d8-d64bf2d708e6","description":"Oopstay","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7cf9-b360-bf651ab34e77","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which Greek god invented the shepherd\'s flute and had a musical contest with Apollo?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Pan\u2019s reed pipes are commonly called panpipes. In the musical contest, Apollo played the lyre.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7657-880d-2193c64a8320","description":"Pan","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7aac-b542-1e571a6f4543","description":"Zeus","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-79be-ab7e-6d7f30b36306","description":"Artemis","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7611-9360-f661a296d154","description":"Athena","correct_answer":fals