answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7e88-8531-a081c7f09a37","description":"Humiliation breeds subservience","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7b56-ac7d-7ce1c27dd901","description":"Humble is the child","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7791-b90b-0c91404dccca","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"What is the meaning of the Latin phrase \'Dum vita est, spes est\'?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"\'Dum vita est, spes est\' is a Latin proverb meaning while there is life there is hope.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7dae-bd6a-b2e29bd172c0","description":"While there is life there is hope","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-74a4-a365-e577b151ccb3","description":"Wisdom is power","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7378-a494-686f0877806e","description":"Every man is the maker of his own fortune","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7d1e-8c51-50129047cced","description":"So it begins","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-794d-a4e2-c519ffd85bf2","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which philosopher famously said \'Entities should not be multiplied unnecessarily\'?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"William of Ockham is associated with the principle commonly called Occam\u2019s razor, a rule of thumb for avoiding unnecessary assumptions.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7c5b-80f2-0db7b8080636","description":"William of Ockham","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7721-9032-f2d06156c518","description":"Denis Diderot","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7e2a-ba05-ee8ec4b5d43c","description":"Jean-Paul Sartre","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7b09-858e-094488978ea2","description":"Spinoza","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7179-9263-1f7624a3f35f","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which philosopher famously said \'Even while they teach, men learn\'?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Seneca the Younger was a Roman statesman as well as a philosopher; his moral essays and letters remain among his best-known works.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-78b3-88bc-497035d21790","description":"Seneca the Younger","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-799f-86bb-c3c44525024b","description":"Thomas Hobbes","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7dd0-9cd2-8a6a433e9727","description":"Ludwig Wittgenstein","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7691-bacd-b728afb93280","description":"Socrates","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-76a2-8a58-b8f78074ca6c","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Who was the ancient Egyptian goddess of the sky and queen of heaven ?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Hathor was worshipped as a sky goddess and known as the Lady of Heaven. She was also associated with love, music, and motherhood.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7ba8-a69e-3aa7165a69a5","description":"Hathor","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-71a3-902c-de9fedeaa06a","description":"Isis","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-76c6-9b20-8ed69f7f7c1b","description":"Set","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7244-8676-936687d0c044","description":"Horus","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-79d7-9fb8-9dc13e17b5e2","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"What is a wide cuff that is folded back and fastened with a cuff link called?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"French cuffs are traditionally considered more formal than button-fastened cuffs and use separate cuff links rather than sewn-on buttons.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7d4d-9b52-8494bf5fce69","description":"A French cuff","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7f01-bacb-19a4ff178686","description":"A button cuff","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-769c-b450-92888958f6f3","description":"A barrel cuff","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7b1a-91c2-85fb227c42d6","description":"A saville cuff","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7913-92d3-0bb8b55836a9","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which philosopher famously said \'What is rational is actual and what is actual is rational\'?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The line appears in the preface to Hegel\u2019s Philosophy of Right, where he explored the relationship between reason and the world.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7a6c-9267-edd51a841a29","description":"G. W. F. Hegel","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-74cd-a7da-017d65b0cdff","description":"William of Ockham","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7fd8-880c-280bbf49d394","description":"Bertrand Russell","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7a79-bc2a-04d6b164ee9b","description":"Democritus","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7fa0-a567-e2fc39cf25cb","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"In 1982, which member of the British royal family gave birth to Prince William?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Princess Diana and Charles also had a younger son, Prince Harry, born in 1984.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7fe7-abb8-bf998a8220a4","description":"Princess Diana","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7331-8cf5-750fbe17a75b","description":"Queen Elizabeth II","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7c40-8ba6-5e1a5a8c6ff8","description":"Camilla Parker Bowles","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7a39-b6fd-5f11a0b56175","description":"Sarah Ferguson","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7b00-a4d0-b151be8ab498","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Berber is a language spoken in which of these countries?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Berber languages are also known as Amazigh, and Morocco recognizes Tamazight as an official language.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7527-8073-fd30769870f5","description":"Morocco","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7449-be0d-c96e87d95c0c","description":"Kenya","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7829-85b3-ca7e069b3c96","description":"Tanzania","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7b30-92ca-f67be95acb50","description":"Sri Lanka","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-77d4-81f6-8480f259b67c","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which philosopher famously said \'Whereof one cannot speak, thereof one must be silent\'?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Ludwig Wittgenstein\u2019s Tractatus Logico-Philosophicus explores the limits of language and thought.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-70dc-b065-8d6b3682c53f","description":"Ludwig Wittgenstein","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7886-b614-8461799ad00f","description":"William of Ockham","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7eb6-9c46-38f0abb16bda","description":"Bertrand Russell","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-77e8-a021-d04b86f7ac26","description":"Immanuel Kant","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-72a6-a828-e9238769da38","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which of these Latin phrases means \'Overcome evil with good\'?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Bono malum superate uses a plural command form, addressing more than one person, and echoes the injunction in Romans 12:21.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-728f-9a21-97687abbae4e","description":"Bono malum superate","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-74ab-a1eb-4c7ffa41c30b","description":"Bona fide","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7219-a878-58d21b0fa2cb","description":"Humilitas occidit superbiam","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7204-b01a-6071a351d5cb","description":"Fortiter et fideliter","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-76f1-8ee7-128895fcbbe9","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which philosopher famously said \'There is only one thing a philosopher can be relied upon to do, and that is to contradict other philosophers\'?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"William James was also a pioneering psychologist. His work helped shape pragmatism, which evaluates ideas partly by their practical consequences.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7de0-83a0-0d97d935ec86","description":"William James","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-70fd-af34-07c6586768f8","description":"Thomas Hobbes","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7457-bf27-a00ac17668fe","description":"Socrates","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7057-8b01-4d00c0d887e3","description":"Martin Heidegger","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7615-8f4b-df098da20789","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"What is the shortest verse in the Bible?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Jesus wept is John 11:35, which describes Jesus mourning at Lazarus\u2019s tomb. It is commonly cited as the shortest verse in English-language Bibles.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7a2e-a75c-c69cc147de17","description":"Jesus wept","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7cae-be2b-8ea213afd109","description":"God spoke","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-779b-ab6b-29fe78dade56","description":"No more","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-72c8-a4ed-2ce0707228db","description":"Hallelujah","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-712f-86af-601ace468cb0","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"In 2002, which US city saw a number of coordinated sniper killings?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The 2002 Beltway sniper attacks took place across the Washington metropolitan area, including suburbs in Maryland and Virginia.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7845-9ce0-f80d972dfb44","description":"Washington, D.C.","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7797-a1df-3f3436a20456","description":"New York City","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-758d-accf-6337a00e1f21","description":"Los Angeles","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-72d3-bd64-b7606b7a1d28","description":"Chicago","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7265-9799-79a615047335","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"How does that Latin phrase \'Pax vobiscum\' translate into English?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"\u201cPeace be with you\u201d is a traditional Christian liturgical greeting, often used during worship.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-77eb-9b8b-677bccec39a0","description":"Peace be with you","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-75a8-9b39-38769ad72ae7","description":"In good faith","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-74c1-991d-549d4c07f4be","description":"And you, Brutus","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7adb-9ec4-9584524bb7ab","description":"Nothing is arduous for the willing","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-797c-bce3-ce832a39d0a2","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"How does that Latin phrase \'Tempora mutantur et nos mutamur in illis\' translate into English?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"\'Tempora mutantur, et nos mutamur in illis\' means times change and we change with them.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-750d-ab60-ea6583973df0","description":"The times are changing, and we change with them","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7087-8629-393f3ab2f9de","description":"What is said is done","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7248-9efb-2fdd755b970e","description":"The act done by me against my will is not my act","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-70be-98d9-742cbe1481a7","description":"Fortune favors the bold","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7ea4-a53d-614ac7e3b66e","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"What is the national animal of Scotland?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The unicorn appears as a supporter on Scotland\u2019s royal coat of arms, often shown chained because it was regarded as wild and untamable.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-72b2-8964-a39678ec49ab","description":"Unicorn","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7aa6-a634-8e88e3a670c3","description":"Lion","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7188-84cc-2a415fccb13a","description":"Dragon","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7039-8382-32b6a9e8233c","description":"Horse","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7969-816f-c619b63883fe","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"What charity organization works to protect the rights of indigenous and tribal peoples?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Survival International campaigns against the forced displacement of Indigenous peoples and defends their rights to their lands and ways of life.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-75f6-a69b-48184fc96ec7","description":"Survival International","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-772d-b701-006c752f1c55","description":"Greenpeace","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7d60-acfe-2902c6b2c567","description":"Amnesty International","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7357-a703-28d61ee5a8a1","description":"The Nature Conservancy","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-715c-8263-6feba5778e30","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which philosopher famously said \'It is undesirable to believe a proposition when there is no ground whatever for supposing it true\'?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Bertrand Russell received the Nobel Prize in Literature for his varied writings, which championed humanitarian ideals and freedom of thought.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7cd1-9e9a-f3621005905d","description":"Bertrand Russell","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-77c3-a08d-aac80c467616","description":"Thomas Hobbes","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-724a-8d36-30d08e19aa34","description":"Jean-Jacques Rousseau","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-71d9-a8a0-9152477c1511","description":"Ludwig Wittgenstein","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-710d-93ea-ab48f4f063a7","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which Norse god acts as the watchman of the gods, guarding the rainbow bridge Bifr\u00f6st?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Heimdall is also described as having exceptionally sharp senses; some accounts say he can hear grass growing.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-77a8-a214-c563de1965ad","description":"Heimdall","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7ead-a7f7-be3e133fa964","description":"Thor","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-79a3-8a89-41ea699ad2e0","description":"Baldur","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7c48-90aa-7b6351f49c5e","description":"Tyr","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7f76-bec1-a70b0caf561c","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which philosopher famously said \'God is not willing to do everything, and thus take away our free will and that share of glory which belongs to us\'?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Niccolo Machiavelli discusses the balance between fortune and human agency in The Prince, where this line appears.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-70e5-920e-945c8f4739bf","description":"Niccolo Machiavelli","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-72ef-9e0e-508f7229cb22","description":"Jean-Paul Sartre","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7834-81a3-acadf52a3b70","description":"Ludwig Wittgenstein","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7dbc-9ede-246fa44b0d5e","description":"Karl Marx","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-757d-abb3-ede020e23483","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which of these Latin phrases means \'Wisdom is power\'?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"In Sapientia potentia est, sapientia is the subject, potentia means power, and est is the verb meaning \u201cis.\u201d","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7b65-ae16-b3ff0bef6d8b","description":"Sapientia potentia est","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-79ed-a12f-3b7ea03bb45a","description":"Hodie mihi, cras tibi","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-736a-b878-2d5d16439ba9","description":"Ego te provoco","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7bad-84f6-5586e037dab4","description":"Melita, domi adsum","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-75b0-aa53-f0ba651eb187","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which of the following describes John Dalton?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"John Dalton proposed that matter is made of indivisible atoms, with each element having its own type. His ideas helped lay the groundwork for modern chemistry.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7b4c-a45a-8e7634a28eb4","description":"Chemist and physicist who ade contributions to atomic theory.","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7e3b-8804-cf7f3f30d197","description":"Industrialist who revolutionised mass-production techniques.","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-73da-9169-e0175538e77c","description":"Confirmed the theory that Earth revolves around The Sun.","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7b7b-b103-e156e2b1db28","description":"38th President of the US.","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-773d-b5e5-8439686a645d","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"What is the name of the flag flown on a short pole at the bow of a ship?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"A jack is flown at the bow, while a ship\u2019s ensign is generally flown at the stern; a burgee commonly identifies a yacht club.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-710d-943b-7ce43653af22","description":"Jack","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7f04-9293-b0c12d304ba5","description":"Ensign","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-72ef-afd0-66ac6575b130","description":"Pennant","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7285-8377-480ed18a9d14","description":"Burgee","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7485-ac33-0b7956679fdd","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"How does that Latin phrase \'Actus me invito factus non est meus actus\' translate into English?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The phrase means \u201cThe act done by me against my will is not my act,\u201d expressing the legal principle that criminal responsibility generally requires voluntary conduct.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-73a3-9c74-e67db779d358","description":"The act done by me against my will is not my act","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7e16-a1c2-3b07b986fd09","description":"To act accidentally is not to act at all","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7d97-a89d-76c0514e498c","description":"Act as if you are always being watched","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7139-b5ef-30367760edc5","description":"The act of an honest man cannot be questioned","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-708c-8a13-2aae099f32a4","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"What is the name of the US Military\'s highest award for valor in combat?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The Medal of Honor is the nation\u2019s highest military decoration, reserved for conspicuous gallantry and intrepidity at risk of life, above and beyond the call of duty.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7a9c-b243-7be7d99225de","description":"Medal of Honor","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7214-b4bf-c77dfb608738","description":"Purple Heart","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7f3a-9a38-44bda2a74872","description":"Bronze Star","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7aac-bbbb-3fc1a90b85f1","description":"Silver Star","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7146-ab13-f2ae661ab4b1","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which philosopher famously said \'We live in the best of all possible worlds\'?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Leibniz argued that a perfect God would create the best possible world among all possible worlds. Voltaire later satirized that optimism in Candide.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7482-92a0-e96e97b48b7c","description":"Gottfried Wilhelm Leibniz","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7b30-9b0c-a36d08fae660","description":"Thomas Hobbes","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7de2-bed9-678d6533e6f2","description":"Denis Diderot","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-70d8-b37e-8717c35f22cc","description":"Ludwig Wittgenstein","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7e38-aa87-88c81e49c662","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"What is the name of the first month of the year in the Islamic calendar?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Muharram is one of four sacred months in Islam. Its name is commonly understood to mean \u201cforbidden,\u201d reflecting a traditional prohibition on warfare during the month.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7ded-a4bd-a761b748c42f","description":"Muharram","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-77df-a247-64b06603ccbd","description":"Ramadan","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7dbe-9fa8-db2fe8964d43","description":"Shawwal","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7d65-9fdd-e73d948dba87","description":"Jumada Al-Awwal","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7d78-bc68-b49ba2002a0e","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which country had its first female prime minister, Kim Campbell, serve in 1993?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Canada\u2019s Kim Campbell served for only 132 days before the Progressive Conservatives lost the 1993 federal election.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-718c-a033-6c553ff2cf77","description":"Canada","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7658-8ab3-c908a0c12b82","description":"United States","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7c27-94e1-d9cb833610b6","description":"United Kingdom","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7212-873e-e13d94a363a6","description":"Australia","correct_answer":false}]},{"i