ian","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7a15-9ffc-df4824af2a45","description":"Dravidian","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-757d-aeec-db9041fd90e5","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"The language \'Sudanese Arabic\' belongs to which language family?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Afroasiatic includes the Semitic branch, which contains Arabic as well as Hebrew and Aramaic.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7e80-a834-d6d9888e36c0","description":"Afroasiatic","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7a79-987d-e021c548386a","description":"Kra\u2013Dai","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-75c9-b16e-e9d1f26f8423","description":"Niger\u2013Congo","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7951-9778-e575a8a1c3b2","description":"Austronesian","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7cf0-9e77-24c1e04e8ec4","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"What is the name of the Hindu scripture that contains the dialogue between Krishna and Arjuna?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The Bhagavad Gita is part of the Mahabharata, framed as a conversation just before battle. It is distinct from the Upanishads, the Ramayana, and the Puranas.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7293-a552-c3be90f2d5d9","description":"The Bhagavad Gita","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7fee-92fb-290a5bf57040","description":"The Upanishads","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7c98-b8c6-b59be2a5f885","description":"The Ramayana","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7f31-b28f-f94a874a1b53","description":"The Puranas","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad6b-7f54-963c-9f5e7e24d0e3","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"What is the name of the Islamic call to prayer?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The adhan is the call to prayer recited by the muezzin to summon Muslims.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad6c-78ab-aef0-7b2a207cca4c","description":"Adhan","correct_an